thread.text:
Changing all four now:
- the dials get plain names (how far the pin and card melt together, how crisp the edge is), or go if they aren't a real choice;
- opening and closing become one continuous motion each, with no hold;
- a "Stay joined" toggle keeps a small gooey neck between the card and the pin after it opens;
- the pin changes shape while the card is open, so the two read as one shape.

The preview updates in place, and I'll reply here when it's ready.

Understood. The leaf rebuilt the goo by hand from the recipe's description, then kept patching it, all without asking you. The demo on the page you linked is live, so its real code can be read straight from it. [Rebuild goo from the live demo](cawco:session/cockpit) is now doing that:
- open the transitions.dev page;
- take the demo element's own markup, filter values, CSS timings and script;
- rebuild the pin's goo on them, swapping only the shapes (pin and card instead of the plus button and its menu);
- delete the hand-made neck and parting code they replace.
It compares the two side by side before landing.

On Material: that was me reaching for a name to explain one rule, that an edge belongs to the whole shape. We don't use it, and I shouldn't have cited it.

And the border you saw when clicking to open and clicking again to close came from the same focus bug as Shift. That fix is shipping now.
